# The dump's `temp` section names the checker variable each hoisted argument is
# held in. A call whose argument no name holds hoists it whatever the callee is:
# a user function, a generic native method (`String.append`, declared
# `function as { T: StringLike.generic } … is native`), or a generic unit member
# (`print`, `io.eprintln`). The generic ones reach the hoist through their own
# leg, which opens a call scope of its own.
#
# Not every argument is hoisted. A bare name and a plain string literal are
# trivial -- a literal is a view over static program memory, and a temporary
# that owned one would free it -- and a projection (`s.stringView`) reaches into
# what its walk pinned, so the pin holds it rather than a temporary.

greet: function {s: String.view} out u64 is {
    return s.length
}

main: function is {
    n: 3
    buf: "x".string
    tail: "t".string
    k: greet s: "\{n}"
    buf.append "\{n}"
    buf.append " tail"
    buf.append tail
    print "\{k}"
    io.eprintln buf.stringView
}
